  "comments": "In 1970, the United States Mint in Denver manufactured 55,843,368 blank planchets to be used to the minting of this coin.<br /><br />\r\nThis type has several variants (narrow/wide dates, thick/thin dates, open/closed 8s), some of which are described below, with the following dates: 1970, 1975, 1977, 1978, 1979, 1980, 1981, 1982 and 1983<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1970</span><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/59c7a7d46a0b6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/59c7a7d46a0b6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1975</span><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/57c03e169d7e6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/57c03e169d7e6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1977</span><br />\r\nThin date variety has wider space between numbers and coin&#039;s rim, space between sideburns and collar, lower mint mark with larger space between &quot;M&quot; and &quot;o,&quot; different hair waves on back, knot on neckerchief, and ornamentation in the neck with &quot;heart-shape&quot; trim (opposite to the &quot;M-shaped&quot; ones in the normal issue).<br />\r\nThe coin with the thick date (first image) has a die error, the top of the 9 in 1977 is partially missing. The other image shows another die error coin, struck with further die degradation. A slightly bigger part of the 9 is missing and the end of the 9 is different as well.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/57c03e2b41658.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/57c03e2b41658.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6505b9cab40a8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6505b9cab40a8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"124\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1978</span><br />\r\nOpen &quot;8&quot; variety has no knot on neckerchief and a higher mint mark.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/57c03e5838b1f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/57c03e5838b1f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1979</span><br />\r\nThick date variety has less detail on hair at back and on the neck ornaments, wrinkles on neckerchief are fused in a single one near halfway to the back, while on the thin date they stay as two until the very tip.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/57c03e4014c99.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/57c03e4014c99.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1980</span><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/59c71f3780ed5.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/59c71f3780ed5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1981</span><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/59c7e77d735ca.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/59c7e77d735ca.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1982 8&#039;s<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62864820e35f3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62864820e35f3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">1983</span><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/59c71f65c0f6a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/59c71f65c0f6a.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a>",
